{"title":"1996 OIM Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a natural number. A cube with edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be divided into 1996 cubes whose edges are also natural numbers. Determine the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A cube with edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be divided at the most into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba37f50c674bcbae995ed1d9dfd4beb5e53c765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> cubes with side 1.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e8be21e9582b514daf57274db91fe19535240f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12^3 &lt; 1996 &lt; 13^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" /> then smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be less or equal to 12.  Now we need to find out if it is possible to divide a cube of edge 13 into 1996 cubes.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bfe02fd316cc75ef7e46a5df389c9d6e62b6334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^3-1996=201$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />, this means that I have 201 extra cubes of side 1.  Now we need to find out if we can if I can combine groups of these into other cubes of larger edge sides until my total of cubes is 1996.  That is, I can combine 8 cubes into a cube of edge 2, 27 cubes into a cube of edge 3, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bb87766bcaaf492fc1be5874b732197f6f0d641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> cubes into a cube of edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and so on...\n</p><p>We can express the volume of the cube as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97de0c935e1e92ef66ad5171f8a200d63fe115f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V=\\sum_{i}^{}2^ik_i=13^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"149\" height=\"48\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0ac59ec3562b84367674cfe6245f223b892913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> is the quantity of cubes of edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, Hence, we want to find solve this equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0ac59ec3562b84367674cfe6245f223b892913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e237f92e14eb9ffbd746d23020e84e62406b9b67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i}^{}k_i=1996$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"106\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4858a281c3f283afbe3a6ca8af0275af584dae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1=13^3=2197$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> with 201 cubes left we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/0091c6b63eb6531558304319a28954feb4b3871c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$201=(25)(8^3)+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" />.  So, we can make 25 cubes of edge 2.  If we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb72004e1c6c7b0782bbf2c7e40dcaad72993c4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />=25 we need to subtract 200 from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and our numbers are now at:  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baa1141feb9af5a2dcdfa06276fd8acd7ceb2de3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1=1997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd1a5aa24e67c68efa2148d24052f4ab463fe2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/217d371e5672279a840ccd168191f8e0ea9c7330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i}^{}k_i=2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"106\" height=\"48\" />.  So we still have 26 cubes more than we need.\n</p><p>So we can take 27 cubes of edge 1 (subtract 27 from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2f57887b2e2f63a617b6a4b7a7d466c26c4342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />) and combine them into one cube of edge three and our new numbers are:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f4ae81ba308843a9ff3ab4dd660820a1626b929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1=1970$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd1a5aa24e67c68efa2148d24052f4ab463fe2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/2/a22eadf9127575f30cb27730ae2010ff26c73b26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_3=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b7f6972bcf0cf9c38f9d67709b34edd5bf8372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i}^{}k_i=1970+25+1=1996$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"238\" height=\"48\" />.  And this proves that we can divide a cube of edge 13 into 1970 cubes of edge 1, plus 25 cubes of edge 2, plus one cube of edge 3.\n</p><p>Since smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is greater than 12, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608f4cbd198d2af6bf20b99fc5e126469e09ec84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> is possible then smallest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is 13.\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe11.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe11.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017020124\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 165/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 344/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5333/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.913      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%   11.913      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26101:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017020124 and revision id 208234. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}